## Create React Native project {% #create-react-project %}

Create a React Native app with the `create-expo-app` command.
The default template sets up an Expo Router app with TypeScript.

```sh
npx create-expo-app@latest ideas-tracker
cd ideas-tracker
```

The template includes example screens. Remove them with the `reset-project` script.
When the script asks if you want to move the existing files to `/example`, enter `n` to delete them.

```sh
npm run reset-project
```

The script creates a blank `src/app` directory with two files:

- `src/app/_layout.tsx` is the root layout. It wraps every screen in the app.
- `src/app/index.tsx` is the first screen of the app.

Expo Router treats every file in `src/app` as a route.
Put the rest of the app code, such as contexts and helpers, in other directories inside `src`.

## Add dependencies {% #add-dependencies %}

Install the React Native Appwrite SDK.

```sh
npx expo install react-native-appwrite react-native-url-polyfill
```
